       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose for depression or anxiety.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is intended, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me that and I can add a note to the order. I'd still recommend confirming it with pharmacy first."
